<% content_for :own_heading, true %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
  <%= render "admin/component_demo/environment_banner" %>

  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <% description = "What a teacher could be shown on /stocks, against real records. " \
                   "Built to decide something, and deleted once decided." %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Trading floor columns", description: description } do %><% end %>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Today, as a teacher</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
        Two columns. <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">StockPolicy#show_holdings?</code>
        requires a student with a persisted portfolio, so the holdings column and the Buy/Sell cell are both
        removed and this is what is left. The header names an exchange the cell does not contain.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-3">
        <%= render "shared/table_container", table_class: "table-fixed" do %>
          <thead>
            <tr class="table-header-row">
              <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left">Company (exchange)</th>
              <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-right w-40">Last price</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% @stocks.first(4).each do |stock| %>
              <tr class="table-body-row">
                <td class="table-body-cell">
                  <div class="flex flex-col">
                    <span class="tw-link"><%= stock.ticker %></span>
                    <span class="text-sm text-slate-600"><%= stock.company_name %></span>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td class="table-body-cell table-body-cell-right">
                  <span class="table-cell-content block"><%= number_to_currency(stock.current_price) %></span>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Proposed</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
        Three additions, all in the columns a student's holdings and actions already occupy, so the table
        gains no width for anyone and nothing changes at 375px.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-3">
        <%= render "shared/table_container", table_class: "table-fixed" do %>
          <thead>
            <tr class="table-header-row">
              <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left">Company</th>
              <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left hidden w-44 lg:table-cell">
                Industry
              </th>
              <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-right w-40">Last price</th>
              <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-right hidden w-44 lg:table-cell">
                Held by
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% @stocks.each do |stock| %>
              <% held = @holdings[stock.id] %>
              <tr class="table-body-row">
                <td class="table-body-cell">
                  <div class="flex flex-col">
                    <%# 2. The exchange, in the identity line - which is what the current header already
                        promises. `KO . NYSE` is how Bloomberg, Yahoo Finance and Google Finance render a
                        security's identity, and stock_exchange is populated on every active stock and shown
                        only on stocks#show today. In the cell rather than a column of its own, so an
                        archived stock without one leaves no gap. %>
                    <span class="flex items-baseline gap-1.5">
                      <span class="tw-link"><%= stock.ticker %></span>
                      <% if stock.stock_exchange.present? %>
                        <span class="text-xs text-slate-600">&middot; <%= stock.stock_exchange %></span>
                      <% end %>
                    </span>
                    <span class="text-sm text-slate-600"><%= stock.company_name %></span>

                    <%# Below lg the Held by figure moves into the primary cell, which is exactly what a
                        student's holdings line already does - the two secondary columns are `hidden` there,
                        and a teacher on a phone would otherwise be back to the two-column page this preview
                        exists to fix. Industry does not follow it: three lines in one cell is a paragraph,
                        and of the three additions it is the one a teacher can most afford to open the stock
                        for. %>
                    <span class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 lg:hidden">
                      <% if held %>
                        Held by <%= held[:holders] %> of <%= @investors %> &middot;
                        <%= share_count(held[:shares]) %> shares
                      <% else %>
                        Nobody owns this yet
                      <% end %>
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </td>

                <%# 3. Industry. Populated on all ten active stocks and on none of the eight archived ones,
                    so it goes on this table only - a column of dashes is not a column. %>
                <td class="table-body-cell hidden lg:table-cell">
                  <span class="table-cell-content"><%= stock.industry %></span>
                </td>

                <td class="table-body-cell table-body-cell-right">
                  <span class="table-cell-content block"><%= number_to_currency(stock.current_price) %></span>
                </td>

                <%# 1. The one question nothing in the app answers: what is my class buying? A figure and
                    the shares under it, not a sentence - the column is scanned down, and "9 of 25 students"
                    repeated ten times is ten copies of the denominator. Zero is stated rather than left
                    blank: "nobody owns this" is information, and an empty cell reads as missing data. %>
                <td class="table-body-cell table-body-cell-right hidden lg:table-cell">
                  <% if held %>
                    <span class="table-cell-content block tabular-nums">
                      <%= held[:holders] %> of <%= @investors %>
                    </span>
                    <span class="mt-0.5 block text-xs text-slate-600 tabular-nums">
                      <%= share_count(held[:shares]) %> shares
                    </span>
                  <% else %>
                    <span class="table-cell-content block text-slate-600">None</span>
                  <% end %>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
        The denominator is students with a <em>portfolio</em>, not students: a student without one cannot
        hold anything, so counting all of them would understate every row by the size of that gap.
        <%= @investors %> here, across <%= pluralize(@classroom_ids.size, "classroom") %>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
